From b6320858a82e265a2902d0b3fc1680a1bebc7f40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garvit Gupta <garvgupt@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 13:11:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Machine Outliner][RISCV] Input section aware machine
 outlining

Currently machine outliner refuses to outline from functions from named section
functions because the callers of the outlined function could potentially be in
multiple different input sections and outlined function can only be in one of
the input section therefore having cross-section calls that breaks the assumption
around the code being all in the same section

This PR fixes the issue by partitioning the candidates of a repeated sequence
by their parent function's input sections and emitting the outlined function
within the same section. An outlined function inherits its parents' input
section.

This is opt-in via `TargetInstrInfo::supportsSectionAwareOutlining()`, which
defaults to false and has been enabled only for RISCV.

Signed-off-by: Garvit Gupta <garvgupt@qti.qualcomm.com>
